{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<cstring>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int N = 65;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nint m, len;\nll n, digits[N];\n\nstruct Mat {\n    int a[35][35];\n    Mat() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n};\n\nMat mul(const Mat& x, const Mat& y) {\n    Mat z;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j)\n            for (int k = 0; k <= m; ++k)\n                z.a[i][j] = (z.a[i][j] + (ll)x.a[i][k] * y.a[k][j] % MOD) % MOD;\n    return z;\n}\n\nMat T[N][35], pref[N][35], suff[N][35], cur;\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%lld%d\", &n, &m);\n    digits[0] = n;\n    while (digits[len]) {\n        digits[len + 1] = digits[len] / m;\n        digits[len] %= m;\n        ++len;\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; ++i) {\n        if (i == 0) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                T[i][j].a[m][m] = 1;\n                for (int a = 0; a < m; ++a) {\n                    if (a != j) {\n                        T[i][j].a[a][a] = 1;\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    for (int b = 0; b <= m; ++b)\n                        T[i][j].a[a][b] = 1;\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                if (j == 0)\n                    T[i][j] = suff[i - 1][0];\n                else\n                    T[i][j] = mul(suff[i - 1][j], pref[i - 1][j - 1]);\n            }\n        }\n        pref[i][0] = T[i][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j)\n            pref[i][j] = mul(pref[i][j - 1], T[i][j]);\n        suff[i][m - 1] = T[i][m - 1];\n        for (int j = m - 2; j >= 0; --j)\n            suff[i][j] = mul(T[i][j], suff[i][j + 1]);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n        cur.a[0][i] = 1;\n    for (int i = len - 1, j = 0; i >= 0; --i) {\n        ll cnt = digits[i];\n        while (cnt--) {\n            cur = mul(cur, T[i][j]);\n            j = (j + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\", cur.a[0][m]);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mul(A, B):\n    n = len(A)\n    p = len(B[0])\n    k = len(B)\n    C = [[0] * p for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(p):\n            s = 0\n            for t in range(k):\n                s = (s + A[i][t] * B[t][j]) % MOD\n            C[i][j] = s\n    return C\n\ndef make_T0(j, m):\n    mat = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    mat[m][m] = 1\n    for a in range(m):\n        if a != j:\n            mat[a][a] = 1\n        else:\n            for b in range(m + 1):\n                mat[a][b] = 1\n    return mat\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n\n    # extract base-m digits from least significant to most significant\n    digits = []\n    temp = n\n    while temp:\n        digits.append(temp % m)\n        temp //= m\n    L = len(digits)\n\n    # if n == 0, digits is empty, L = 0\n    if L == 0:\n        # cur is a row vector of all ones, output element at column m\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    # T[i][j] for i in 0..L-1, j in 0..m-1\n    T = [ [None] * m for _ in range(L) ]\n    pref = [ [None] * m for _ in range(L) ]\n    suff = [ [None] * m for _ in range(L) ]\n\n    for i in range(L):\n        if i == 0:\n            for j in range(m):\n                T[i][j] = make_T0(j, m)\n        else:\n            for j in range(m):\n                if j == 0:\n                    T[i][j] = suff[i-1][0]\n                else:\n                    T[i][j] = mul(suff[i-1][j], pref[i-1][j-1])\n\n        # compute prefix products\n        pref[i][0] = T[i][0]\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            pref[i][j] = mul(pref[i][j-1], T[i][j])\n\n        # compute suffix products\n        suff[i][m-1] = T[i][m-1]\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            suff[i][j] = mul(T[i][j], suff[i][j+1])\n\n    # cur is a row vector (1 x (m+1)) initialized to all ones\n    cur = [[1] * (m + 1)]\n\n    j = 0\n    for i in range(L-1, -1, -1):\n        cnt = digits[i]\n        for _ in range(cnt):\n            cur = mul(cur, T[i][j])\n            j = (j + 1) % m\n\n    print(cur[0][m])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00318068522028625, -0.0005530973430722952, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.3470558769768104e-05, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -0.5733453631401062, -0.0016822961624711752, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -2.3364747903542593e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.2993287444114685, -0.00045170116936787963, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.3132617473602295, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.2900969088077545, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.